<body><div class=WordSection1><p class=inst>Sardar Vallabhbhai National Institute of Technology (SVNIT), Surat</p><p class=dept>Department of Artificial Intelligence</p><p class=course>Agentic AI (IA462) &mdash; Semester VIII</p><hr><table class=g><tr><th>Name</th><th>Roll No.</th><th>Experiment</th><th>Date</th></tr><tr><td>&nbsp;</td><td>U23AI042</td><td>1</td><td>13 August 2026</td></tr></table><h1>Experiment 1</h1><h1 class=sub>Simple Reflex (Reactive) Agent &mdash; The Vacuum-Cleaner World</h1><h2>Aim</h2><p>To implement a reactive agent that maps percepts directly to actions through condition&ndash;action rules, and to measure its behaviour with a performance score in a simulated environment.</p><h2>Theory</h2><p>An agent is anything that perceives its environment through sensors and acts upon it through actuators. The <i>simple reflex agent</i> is the smallest architecture that still earns the name. It holds a fixed set of condition&ndash;action rules, matches the current percept against the conditions, and executes the action of the rule that fires. It stores no history, builds no model of the world and performs no look-ahead, so its behaviour is a pure function of the percept it is looking at at this instant: the same percept always produces the same action, whatever happened before.</p><p>Russell and Norvig's vacuum-cleaner world is the standard testbed for this architecture. There are two squares, A and B; each is either Clean or Dirty; the agent occupies one of them and can Suck, move Left, move Right, or do nothing. Cleaning is rewarded and movement costs energy, so the agent cannot simply thrash about and still score well.</p><p>This experiment also fixes the agent&ndash;environment interface that every later experiment reuses. The environment object owns the truth: the dirt status of both squares, the agent's location and the score. It exposes exactly two operations to the outside world &mdash; <span class=m>percept()</span>, which returns what the sensors can see, and <span class=m>execute(action)</span>, which applies an actuator command and returns the reward it earned. The agent is a plain Python function that receives the percept and returns an action; it never reads the environment's attributes. Everything the agent knows, it knows because it was told through a percept.</p><p>The instructive part of the experiment is the failure mode. Because the percept <span class=m>(A, Clean)</span> carries no information about square B, the rule table must map it to one fixed action. Mapping it to <i>Right</i> makes the agent oscillate for ever once both squares are clean, bleeding one point per step; mapping it to <i>NoOp</i> makes the agent freeze on square A and never discover that B is dirty. Both runs are reproduced below. The fix is not a better rule table &mdash; it is internal state, which is Experiment 2.</p><p class=cap>Table 1. PEAS description of the task environment.</p><table class=g><tr><th style='width:25%'>PEAS component</th><th style='width:75%'>Specification for this experiment</th></tr><tr><td>Performance measure</td><td>+10 for each successful Suck and &minus;1 for every movement (energy cost), as prescribed by the algorithm. The PEAS-level measure of the manual &mdash; +1 for each clean square at each time step &mdash; is also tracked, in the column <span class=m>CleanCredit</span>, so that the two views of &quot;performance&quot; can be compared.</td></tr><tr><td>Environment</td><td>Two squares A and B, each Clean or Dirty; deterministic, static (until Exercise 3), discrete, and fully observable only locally &mdash; the agent sees the square it stands on and nothing else.</td></tr><tr><td>Actuators</td><td>Suck, Left, Right, NoOp</td></tr><tr><td>Sensors</td><td>Location sensor and dirt sensor, giving the percept (location, status)</td></tr></table><p class=cap>Table 2. The condition&ndash;action rule table implemented in <span class=m>simple_reflex_agent()</span>.</p><table class=g><tr><th style='width:10%'>Rule</th><th style='width:55%'>Condition (percept)</th><th style='width:35%'>Action</th></tr><tr><td>R1</td><td>(any square, Dirty)</td><td>Suck</td></tr><tr><td>R2</td><td>(A, Clean)</td><td>Right</td></tr><tr><td>R3</td><td>(B, Clean)</td><td>Left</td></tr></table><h2>Algorithm</h2><ol><li>Build an environment class holding the dirt status of both locations, the agent's location and a performance score.</li><li>Implement <span class=m>percept()</span>, returning (location, status), and <span class=m>execute(action)</span>, applying Suck / Left / Right with rewards +10 and &minus;1.</li><li>Implement the agent as a pure function: if the current square is dirty then Suck, otherwise move to the other square.</li><li>Run the perception&ndash;action loop for a fixed number of steps: perceive, decide, act, score the time step.</li><li>Report the initial state, the percept&ndash;action trace of every step, and the final state with the performance score.</li></ol><p>The loop itself is four lines, and they are the whole of agency at this level:</p><pre class=code style='font-size:9pt'>for t in range(1, steps + 1):
    percept = env.percept()          # 1. perceive
    action  = agent(percept)         # 2. decide  (rule table)
    reward  = env.execute(action)    # 3. act
    env.tick_clean_credit()          # 4. score the time step</pre><br style='page-break-before:always'><h2>Procedure and Result</h2><h3>Program &mdash; exp1_reflex_agent.py</h3><pre class=code style='font-size:7.5pt'>&quot;&quot;&quot;
Experiment 1 - Simple Reflex (Reactive) Agent : The Vacuum-Cleaner World
Agentic AI (IA462), Semester VIII - SVNIT Surat

Reference program.  Python standard library only; no agent framework is used
(Rules and Regulations, clause 3.1).  Every part of the perception-action loop
- the environment, the percept, the condition-action rules and the driver loop
- appears explicitly below.

Design note (agent-environment separation):
    The environment owns the TRUE state (dirt in both squares, agent location,
    score).  It exposes exactly two methods to the outside world:
        percept()        -&gt; (location, status)   what the sensors report
        execute(action)  -&gt; reward              what the actuators do
    The agent is a pure function.  It receives nothing but the percept and
    returns nothing but an action.  It has no memory and no model of the world.
&quot;&quot;&quot;

CLEAN = &quot;Clean&quot;
DIRTY = &quot;Dirty&quot;

SUCK, LEFT, RIGHT, NOOP = &quot;Suck&quot;, &quot;Left&quot;, &quot;Right&quot;, &quot;NoOp&quot;

REWARD_SUCK = +10      # cleaning is rewarded          (Algorithm, step 2)
REWARD_MOVE = -1       # every movement costs energy   (Algorithm, step 2)


# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# 1. The environment: it holds the true state of the world.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
class VacuumEnvironment:
    &quot;&quot;&quot;Two squares, A and B, each Clean or Dirty.&quot;&quot;&quot;

    def __init__(self, status=None, location=&quot;A&quot;):
        # status maps square name -&gt; CLEAN / DIRTY
        self.status = dict(status) if status else {&quot;A&quot;: DIRTY, &quot;B&quot;: DIRTY}
        self.location = location
        self.score = 0          # task performance measure (+10 suck, -1 move)
        self.clean_credit = 0   # PEAS measure: +1 per clean square per step

    # -- sensors ------------------------------------------------------------ #
    def percept(self):
        &quot;&quot;&quot;All the agent is ever allowed to see.&quot;&quot;&quot;
        return (self.location, self.status[self.location])

    # -- actuators ---------------------------------------------------------- #
    def execute(self, action):
        &quot;&quot;&quot;Apply an action to the world and return the reward it earned.&quot;&quot;&quot;
        reward = 0
        if action == SUCK:
            if self.status[self.location] == DIRTY:
                self.status[self.location] = CLEAN
                reward = REWARD_SUCK
        elif action == LEFT:
            self.location = &quot;A&quot;
            reward = REWARD_MOVE
        elif action == RIGHT:
            self.location = &quot;B&quot;
            reward = REWARD_MOVE
        elif action == NOOP:
            reward = 0
        else:
            raise ValueError(&quot;unknown action: %r&quot; % (action,))

        self.score += reward
        return reward

    # -- book-keeping ------------------------------------------------------- #
    def tick_clean_credit(self):
        &quot;&quot;&quot;+1 for each square that is clean at this time step (PEAS measure).&quot;&quot;&quot;
        gained = sum(1 for s in self.status.values() if s == CLEAN)
        self.clean_credit += gained
        return gained

    def world_state(self):
        return &quot;A=%-5s  B=%-5s  agent@%s&quot; % (
            self.status[&quot;A&quot;], self.status[&quot;B&quot;], self.location)


# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# 2. The agent: a pure function from percept to action.  No internal state.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
def simple_reflex_agent(percept):
    &quot;&quot;&quot;Condition-action rules of Russell &amp; Norvig&#x27;s reflex vacuum agent.

        if status is Dirty      -&gt; Suck
        else if location is A   -&gt; Right
        else                    -&gt; Left
    &quot;&quot;&quot;
    location, status = percept
    if status == DIRTY:
        return SUCK
    elif location == &quot;A&quot;:
        return RIGHT
    else:
        return LEFT


def noop_when_clean_agent(percept):
    &quot;&quot;&quot;A second, equally memoryless rule table, used in RUN 4 as a control.

        if status is Dirty -&gt; Suck   else -&gt; NoOp

    It removes the oscillation, and with it the agent&#x27;s only way of ever
    reaching the other square.
    &quot;&quot;&quot;
    location, status = percept
    return SUCK if status == DIRTY else NOOP


# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# 3. The perception-action loop.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
def run(env, agent, steps):
    print(&quot;Initial state : %s&quot; % env.world_state())
    print(&quot;Performance   : score = %d&quot; % env.score)
    print()
    header = &quot;%-5s | %-16s | %-6s | %-25s | %-7s | %-6s | %s&quot; % (
        &quot;Step&quot;, &quot;Percept&quot;, &quot;Action&quot;, &quot;Resulting world state&quot;,
        &quot;Reward&quot;, &quot;Score&quot;, &quot;CleanCredit&quot;)
    print(header)
    print(&quot;-&quot; * len(header))

    for t in range(1, steps + 1):
        percept = env.percept()          # 1. perceive
        action = agent(percept)          # 2. decide  (condition-action rules)
        reward = env.execute(action)     # 3. act
        env.tick_clean_credit()          # 4. environment scores the time step

        print(&quot;%-5d | %-16s | %-6s | %-25s | %+7d | %+6d | %d&quot; % (
            t, &quot;(%s, %s)&quot; % percept, action, env.world_state(),
            reward, env.score, env.clean_credit))

    print()
    print(&quot;Final state   : %s&quot; % env.world_state())
    print(&quot;Performance   : score = %d   (clean-square credit = %d over %d steps)&quot;
          % (env.score, env.clean_credit, steps))
    return env.score


if __name__ == &quot;__main__&quot;:
    print(&quot;=&quot; * 96)
    print(&quot;EXPERIMENT 1 - SIMPLE REFLEX AGENT - VACUUM-CLEANER WORLD&quot;)
    print(&quot;=&quot; * 96)
    print()

    print(&quot;&gt;&gt;&gt; RUN 1 : both squares initially Dirty, agent starts at A, 10 steps&quot;)
    print()
    env = VacuumEnvironment(status={&quot;A&quot;: DIRTY, &quot;B&quot;: DIRTY}, location=&quot;A&quot;)
    run(env, simple_reflex_agent, steps=10)

    print()
    print(&quot;=&quot; * 96)
    print(&quot;&gt;&gt;&gt; RUN 2 : only B dirty, agent starts at A, 10 steps&quot;)
    print()
    env2 = VacuumEnvironment(status={&quot;A&quot;: CLEAN, &quot;B&quot;: DIRTY}, location=&quot;A&quot;)
    run(env2, simple_reflex_agent, steps=10)

    print()
    print(&quot;=&quot; * 96)
    print(&quot;&gt;&gt;&gt; RUN 3 : effect of the horizon - same start, increasing step budget&quot;)
    print()
    print(&quot;%-8s | %-12s | %s&quot; % (&quot;Steps&quot;, &quot;Final score&quot;, &quot;Clean-square credit&quot;))
    print(&quot;-&quot; * 48)
    for n in (2, 5, 10, 20, 50, 100):
        e = VacuumEnvironment(status={&quot;A&quot;: DIRTY, &quot;B&quot;: DIRTY}, location=&quot;A&quot;)
        for _ in range(n):
            e.execute(simple_reflex_agent(e.percept()))
            e.tick_clean_credit()
        print(&quot;%-8d | %-12d | %d&quot; % (n, e.score, e.clean_credit))
    print()
    print(&quot;The score falls by 1 for every step after the world is clean:&quot;)
    print(&quot;the reflex agent oscillates A -&gt; B -&gt; A -&gt; ... for ever.&quot;)

    print()
    print(&quot;=&quot; * 96)
    print(&quot;&gt;&gt;&gt; RUN 4 : control - can a different rule table fix it without memory?&quot;)
    print(&quot;            rules: Dirty -&gt; Suck, Clean -&gt; NoOp;  world: only B dirty&quot;)
    print()
    env4 = VacuumEnvironment(status={&quot;A&quot;: CLEAN, &quot;B&quot;: DIRTY}, location=&quot;A&quot;)
    run(env4, noop_when_clean_agent, steps=10)
    print()
    print(&quot;It stops paying the movement cost, but it never reaches B either:&quot;)
    print(&quot;B stays dirty for ever.  The percept (A, Clean) has to be mapped to&quot;)
    print(&quot;exactly one action, and the same percept occurs both when the world&quot;)
    print(&quot;is finished and when B is still dirty.  No memoryless rule table can&quot;)
    print(&quot;be right in both cases - the limitation is the architecture, not the&quot;)
    print(&quot;choice of rules.&quot;)</pre><br style='page-break-before:always'><h3>Output</h3><p class=cap>Snapshot of the console output (Python 3.12.1 on Windows (AMD64), executed 13 August 2026, 00:25).</p><pre class=out style='font-size:6.5pt'>================================================================================================
EXPERIMENT 1 - SIMPLE REFLEX AGENT - VACUUM-CLEANER WORLD
================================================================================================

&gt;&gt;&gt; RUN 1 : both squares initially Dirty, agent starts at A, 10 steps

Initial state : A=Dirty  B=Dirty  agent@A
Performance   : score = 0

Step  | Percept          | Action | Resulting world state     | Reward  | Score  | CleanCredit
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1     | (A, Dirty)       | Suck   | A=Clean  B=Dirty  agent@A |     +10 |    +10 | 1
2     | (A, Clean)       | Right  | A=Clean  B=Dirty  agent@B |      -1 |     +9 | 2
3     | (B, Dirty)       | Suck   | A=Clean  B=Clean  agent@B |     +10 |    +19 | 4
